# Operator installs under a root-controlled directory, root:root mode0600.
# Examples only; never copy real secrets into git/chat/reports. No inline comments.
# No secrets here (9h): the bot reads DATABASE_URL (bfx_bot role), BFX_ADMIN_TOKEN,
# BFX_ADMIN_READ_TOKEN, BFX_VAULT_KEK and TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN only from its secret files
# /opt/bfx/runtime/secrets/bot/<KEY> (root:4600 0640; docs/runbooks/deploy.md "Secret
# files"); the same keys here are ignored and named in a boot warning.
# Operator alerts from the bot (T8): the chat id, same as /opt/bfx/runtime/notify.env.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Error tracking (Sentry project bfx-backend; webapi.env carries the same DSN).
# Empty = off. docs/runbooks/operations.md "Error tracking".
SENTRY_DSN=

# Account identity (nonsecret; the retired release bundle used to inject it).
# Non-secret bot settings come from deploy/vm/live.env at the deployed commit.
BFX_EXCHANGE_ACCOUNT_ID=replace-with-canonical-exchange-account-uuid
# Money is decided only by the applied CapitalPolicy. Do not copy .env.runtime or
# BFX_CANARY_*/amount/cap/buffer/scope legacy keys.
# The separate protected webapi.env carries SENTRY_DSN (same as here) and the tailnet
# ingress keys; the web API's secrets are its files secrets/webapi/DATABASE_URL (bfx_webapi)
# and secrets/webapi/BFX_ADMIN_READ_TOKEN (the SAME value as the bot's). It never gets
# BFX_ADMIN_TOKEN or BFX_VAULT_KEK, as a key or a file: it refuses to start with either.
# Ingress keys: BFX_OPERATOR_TAILNET_USER_ID, BFX_WEBAPI_ALLOWED_HOSTS, BFX_FE_SENTRY_DSN
# (core/settings.py IngressSettings).
# bfx-deploy rejects values with `$`, surrounding quotes or ` #`, and loader/
# identity keys (PYTHONPATH, LD_*, BFX_IMAGE_DIGEST, ...). Procedure:
# docs/runbooks/deploy.md; first install: docs/runbooks/fresh-host-setup.md
